# Pavel Chekov, First Posting: "If you would draw a card, you may instead choose land or nonland and reveal cards from the
# top of your library until you reveal a card of the chosen kind. Put that card into your hand and put all other cards
# revealed this way on the bottom of your library in a random order" (CR 121.6, 614.1a, 701.20). Bot1 casts it on turn 1
# and takes the effect on its turn 3 draw, choosing land: a Grizzly Bears is on top, so it and the Island under it are
# revealed, the Island goes into the hand and the Bears to the bottom - two cards left the library and only one reached the
# hand, so the draw itself did not happen. Turn 5 declines and draws normally; turn 7 chooses nonland and takes the Bears
# past an Island. Bot2's library is never touched.

